###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Continuity
:Continuity rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                   "Rob Brennan" ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
            rdfs:comment "The probability that the specified PNT system performance will be maintained for the duration of a phase of operation, presuming that the PNT system was available at the beginning of that phase of operation."@en ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
            rdfs:label "Continuity"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The probability that the specified PNT system performance will be maintained for the duration of a phase of operation, presuming that the PNT system was available at the beginning of that phase of operation."@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Continuity"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#ContractualContext
:ContractualContext rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                           "Rob Brennan" ;
                    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-04-08"^^xsd:date ;
                    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO27000:2037" ;
                    rdfs:comment "A contextual theory of contract law also recognizes a number of phenomena. First, contract interpretation, through the lens of context, should be used to regulate influences that question the purity of the freedom of contract upon which most agreements are based."@en ;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                    rdfs:label "Contractual Context"@en ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A contextual theory of contract law also recognizes a number of phenomena. First, contract interpretation, through the lens of context, should be used to regulate influences that question the purity of the freedom of contract upon which most agreements are based."@en ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Contractual Context"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Control
