###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#DecisionMakingProcessContext
:DecisionMakingProcessContext rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                                     "Rob Brennan" ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-04-08"^^xsd:date ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO27000:2033" ;
                              rdfs:comment "The decision-making process in cybersecurity is a critical aspect of organizational governance, risk management, and resilience. By following a systematic approach to identify objectives, assess risks, evaluate options, and implement effective measures, organizations can make informed decisions that mitigate cyber threats, protect assets, and support business objectives."@en ;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                              rdfs:label "Decision making process context"@en ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The decision-making process in cybersecurity is a critical aspect of organizational governance, risk management, and resilience. By following a systematic approach to identify objectives, assess risks, evaluate options, and implement effective measures, organizations can make informed decisions that mitigate cyber threats, protect assets, and support business objectives."@en ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Decision making process context"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Defence
:Defence rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
