###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#IdentityAndAccessManagement
:IdentityAndAccessManagement rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                                    "Rob Brennan" ;
                             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
                             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
                             rdfs:comment "Access Management is the set of practices that enables only those permitted the ability to perform an action on a particular resource. The three most common Access Management services you encounter every day perhaps without realizing it are: Policy Administration, Authentication, and Authorization."@en ;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                             rdfs:label "Identity and access management"@en ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Access Management is the set of practices that enables only those permitted the ability to perform an action on a particular resource. The three most common Access Management services you encounter every day perhaps without realizing it are: Policy Administration, Authentication, and Authorization."@en ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Identity and access management"@en .


