###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#InformationProtection
:InformationProtection rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                              "Rob Brennan" ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
                       rdfs:comment "Ensur(ing) that any data contained in a resource is not available when the resource is de-allocated from one object and reallocated to a different object."@en ;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                       rdfs:label "Information protection"@en ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ensur(ing) that any data contained in a resource is not available when the resource is de-allocated from one object and reallocated to a different object."@en ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Information protection"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#InformationSecurity
