###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#MeasurementMethod
:MeasurementMethod rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                          "Rob Brennan" ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-04-08"^^xsd:date ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO27000:2018" ;
                   rdfs:comment "logical sequence of operations, described generically, used in quantifying an attribute with respect to a specified scale Note 1 to entry: The type of measurement method depends on the nature of the operations used to quantify an attribute (3.4). Two types can be distinguished: — subjective: quantification involving human judgment; and — objective: quantification based on numerical rules."@en ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                   rdfs:label "Measurement method"@en ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> :Measurement ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "logical sequence of operations, described generically, used in quantifying an attribute with respect to a specified scale Note 1 to entry: The type of measurement method depends on the nature of the operations used to quantify an attribute (3.4). Two types can be distinguished: — subjective: quantification involving human judgment; and — objective: quantification based on numerical rules."@en ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Measurement method"@en .


