###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Protect
:Protect rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                "Rob Brennan" ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
         rdfs:comment "Develop and implement safeguards to deliver critical infrastructure services."@en ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
         rdfs:label "Protect"@en ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Develop and implement safeguards to deliver critical infrastructure services."@en ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Protect"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Protection
:Protection rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                   "Rob Brennan" ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
            rdfs:comment "In the context of systems security engineering, a control objective that applies across all types of asset types and the corresponding consequences of loss. A system protection capability is a system control objective and a system design problem. The solution to the problem is optimized through a balanced proactive strategy and a reactive strategy that is not limited to prevention. The strategy also encompasses avoiding asset loss and consequences; detecting asset loss and consequences; minimizing (i.e., limiting, containing, restricting) asset loss and consequences; responding to asset loss and consequences; recovering from asset loss and consequences; and forecasting or predicting asset loss and consequences."@en ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
            rdfs:label "Protection"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In the context of systems security engineering, a control objective that applies across all types of asset types and the corresponding consequences of loss. A system protection capability is a system control objective and a system design problem. The solution to the problem is optimized through a balanced proactive strategy and a reactive strategy that is not limited to prevention. The strategy also encompasses avoiding asset loss and consequences; detecting asset loss and consequences; minimizing (i.e., limiting, containing, restricting) asset loss and consequences; responding to asset loss and consequences; recovering from asset loss and consequences; and forecasting or predicting asset loss and consequences."@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Protection"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Recover
:Recover rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                "Rob Brennan" ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
         rdfs:comment "Develop and implement the appropriate activities to maintain plans for  resilience and to restore any capabilities or services that were  impaired due to a cyber security event."@en ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
         rdfs:label "Recover"@en ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Develop and implement the appropriate activities to maintain plans for  resilience and to restore any capabilities or services that were  impaired due to a cyber security event."@en ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Recover"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#RegulatoryEnvironment
:RegulatoryEnvironment rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                              "Rob Brennan" ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-04-08"^^xsd:date ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO27000:2039" ;
                       rdfs:comment "that part of the firm's external marketing environment on which legal and political forces act to change regulations which affect the marketing effort"@en ;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                       rdfs:label "Regulatory environment"@en ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "that part of the firm's external marketing environment on which legal and political forces act to change regulations which affect the marketing effort"@en ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Regulatory environment"@en .


