###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Requirement
:Requirement rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                    "Rob Brennan" ;
             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-04-08"^^xsd:date ;
             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO27000:2018" ;
             rdfs:comment "need or expectation that is stated, generally implied or obligatory Note 1 to entry: “Generally implied” means that it is custom or common practice for the organization and interested parties that the need or expectation under consideration is implied. Note 2 to entry: A specified requirement is one that is stated, for example in documented information."@en ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
             rdfs:label "Requirement"@en ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "need or expectation that is stated, generally implied or obligatory Note 1 to entry: “Generally implied” means that it is custom or common practice for the organization and interested parties that the need or expectation under consideration is implied. Note 2 to entry: A specified requirement is one that is stated, for example in documented information."@en ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Requirement"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#ResidualRisk
:ResidualRisk rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                     "Rob Brennan" ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-04-08"^^xsd:date ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO27000:2018" ;
              rdfs:comment "risk (3.61) remaining after risk treatment (3.72) Note 1 to entry: Residual risk can contain unidentified risk. Note 2 to entry: Residual risk can also be referred to as “retained risk”."@en ;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
              rdfs:label "Residual risk"@en ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> :Risk ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "risk (3.61) remaining after risk treatment (3.72) Note 1 to entry: Residual risk can contain unidentified risk. Note 2 to entry: Residual risk can also be referred to as “retained risk”."@en ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Residual risk"@en .


###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#Resilience
:Resilience rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                   "Rob Brennan" ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
            rdfs:comment "The ability of an information system to continue to: (i) operate under adverse conditions or stress, even if in a degraded or debilitated state, while maintaining essential operational capabilities; and (ii) recover to an effective operational posture in a time frame consistent with mission needs."@en ;
            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
            rdfs:label "Resilience"@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ability of an information system to continue to: (i) operate under adverse conditions or stress, even if in a degraded or debilitated state, while maintaining essential operational capabilities; and (ii) recover to an effective operational posture in a time frame consistent with mission needs."@en ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlTerminology#> ;
            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Resilience"@en .


